    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Yordan Alvarez** (77.75) and **Trea Turner** (76.09) headline the Zurich Zebras lineup as our high-ceiling anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite xwOBA of 0.476 against Rocker, while **Trea Turner**\u2014our primary engine for scarcity-driven stolen base production\u2014enjoys a massive park boost and a favorable matchup against Bradish. Close behind, **Kyle Schwarber** (75.70) presents a premium play; his 16% park adjustment significantly elevates his profile, making him a cornerstone in today's 5x5 construction despite the inherent risk of a high-strikeout matchup. **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (66.27) also deserve mention, as both capitalize on high-order positioning (leadoff) and favorable platoon splits against Scherzer and Cole, respectively, despite the latter battling a \"wind in\" factor that slightly tempered his base projection.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (38.99) and **Pedro Ramirez** (38.70), both of whom fell just short of our mandatory 40.0 efficiency floor. **Chase Meidroth** was the primary consideration for the MI slot, but the optimizer ultimately favored the platoon edge of **Jacob Gonzalez** (40.03), who narrowly cleared the threshold. While **Chase Meidroth** projects as a contact-steady asset, his poor park factor and the SP skill of Jax created a ceiling mismatch compared to our starting infield. We remain disciplined in keeping **Christian Yelich** and **Hyeseong Kim** on the bench due to their current inactive status, ensuring we optimize our game caps for the active contributors who can secure us the win in the steals and power categories. \n\nRisks today center largely on the pitching quality facing our bats; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Pedro Ramirez** are fighting against a tough environment with Cole on the mound, and the \"wind in\" warning adds a layer of volatility for our fly-ball hitters. Conversely, we expect a potential offensive outburst from **Dillon Dingler** (61.92) and **Junior Caminero** (67.34), both of whom have strong dynamic platoon advantages today. We are proceeding with this configuration to maximize our leverage in the SB category while maintaining the power floor required to compete in a tight Roto race.",
